95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (Many schools still conduct student council elections using traditional paper ballots and manual vote counting. This process is time-consuming, often taking hours or even days to complete, especially in schools with a large number of students. Manual counting is also cause to human error, such as miscounted votes, illegible handwriting, which can lead to inaccurate results.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (In addition, the traditional system lacks transparency, since students have no way to verify how votes were counted, which can lead to doubts about the fairness of the election. There is also no reliable way to prevent students from voting more than once, since paper-based systems depend heavily on manual monitoring.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (These issues can result in delayed the results,disputes over results, and reduced trust the process.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
